      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "DEXTERS DONE (2) drew wide last start and was safely held, beaten 50 metres into seventh at this track over 1740m. A nice draw on the front line should ensure a cosy run. Finds a suitable assignment and can turn things around. FRITH IN FLIGHT (11) went back last start then made a long searching run to finish 11 metres from the winner in third at this track over 1740m, that effort following a good win at this track the run prior. Beautifully placed and is sure to play a major role. YELLOW RIVER (7) was beaten 17 metres on debut five-and-a-half months ago over 1758m at Leeton. First-up since that run and has plenty of scope for improvement. BIG NELSON (9) is a two-year-old colt from the Nicholas Hargraves stable on debut. Trial winner who looks above average and is sure to prove tough to beat.",
